<ansi fg="black-bold">.:</ansi> <ansi fg="magenta">Help for </ansi><ansi fg="command">pagination</ansi>

A long answer, such as a help page or a list, stops when it fills your
screen. The last line then says which page you are on, for example
"Page 1 of 3: Enter, q to stop".

<ansi fg="yellow">While it is stopped:</ansi>

::rows
  <ansi fg="command">Enter</ansi>              Show the next page.
  <ansi fg="command">q</ansi>                  Stop reading. The rest is skipped.
  any command        Your command runs, and the rest is skipped.
::

<ansi fg="yellow">Turn it on or off:</ansi>

::rows
  <ansi fg="command">set pagesize</ansi>       Show your page size now.
  <ansi fg="command">set pagesize auto</ansi>  Pages follow the height of your screen.
                     This is the default.
  <ansi fg="command">set pagesize off</ansi>   Never stop. Everything shows at once.
  <ansi fg="command">set pagesize 30</ansi>    Stop every 30 lines. Any number from
                     10 to 200 works.
::

With a screen reader, <ansi fg="command">auto</ansi> stops every 20 lines.

::rows
<ansi fg="magenta-bold">See also:</ansi>  <ansi fg="command">help set</ansi>
::
